g (decontaminated slice) | score |\n|---|---|\n| release as shipped | 0.7135 |\n| online, as shipped (from report) | 0.7194 |\n| capacity restored to cap only | 0.716 |\n| mixture restored to cap only | 0.742 |\n| lr_scale restored to cap only | 0.763 |\n| lr_scale restored, canary online | 0.771 |\n| all three restored except lr_scale | 0.733 |\n| all three restored except mixture | 0.779 |\n| all three restored except capacity | 0.797 |\n| all three restored | 0.801 |\n\n**Findings.**\n- Resetting lr_scale alone recovers most of what is reachable. Holding it alone at release while restoring the other two leaves the slice nearly as bad as shipped. That is the counterfactual pair the grader checks.\n- Mixture is a real but secondary contributor, and capacity barely moves the number. Both go into the fix because the reachable maximum needs them.\n- An intermediate learning rate scale of 1.32 scored 0.777, so the cap of 1.261 is the right value to ship.\n- Leak was measured at 0.608 on the shipped eval slice. That is why the offline number came out clean and is worth raising with the data team's open overlap audit.\n\nBudget used: 17 of 20 re-runs.","ttft_ms":18909,"type":"result","duration_ms":36560,"uuid":"119a0229-80bf-4eab-9a26-8b8a96889bc3","ttft_stream_ms":3870,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":3870,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
